  "Notes": "Achromatic Fresnel rhomb, unsymmetrical coatings (Table III column c): reflecting surface (2) carries 100 A MgF2\nSpecification: Trim layer: together with surface (1) the rhomb gives 90 deg from 214 to 546 nm; in production its thickness (~100 A, held to 10 A) was chosen after measuring the rhomb with surface (1) coated.\nReported: Table III column c: total of both surfaces 87.0, 88.6, 90.5, 90.75, 90.0, 89.1 deg at 546, 405, 334, 289, 248, 214 nm (see Clapham1969-rhomb-c-surface1).\nNotes: Single MgF2 film on silica, TIR at 54 deg. Silica (Spectrosil synthetic fused silica) index is not printed; database SiO2 is used. A check with n = 1.460 at 546 nm reproduces the uncoated rhomb column a (84.55 deg for two reflections at 54 deg). Table III wavelengths 546, 405, 334, 289, 248, 214 nm. Recomputation at 546 nm with n_silica = 1.46 gives 41.57 deg (bare surface 42.28 deg).\nLayers from Table III footnote c (p. 1970); text p. 1971-1972; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
